---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { PROFILE } from '../data/profile';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Accessibility statement"
  description="ORIZ.IN's accessibility goals, implemented features, known limitations, and how to report a barrier."
  lastUpdated="25 October 2026"
>
  <p>
    ORIZ.IN aims to be usable by people with a wide range of abilities. This
    statement describes the target, the practices used, and the limitations
    that remain. It is not a claim of full conformance or an independent
    certification.
  </p>

  <h2>Target</h2>
  <p>
    The site targets WCAG 2.2 Level AA where practical. Some content and
    browser-dependent controls may not meet every criterion in every browser,
    and complex interactive tools need more than an automated check.
  </p>

  <h2>What the site does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Uses semantic HTML landmarks, headings, lists, tables, and form labels.</li>
    <li>Provides a skip-to-content link and visible keyboard focus styles.</li>
    <li>Supports keyboard operation of navigation, search, menus, and tool controls.</li>
    <li>Respects <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> and avoids unnecessary animation.</li>
    <li>Provides light and dark themes with tested color tokens.</li>
    <li>Uses responsive layouts that reflow without horizontal scrolling except in deliberately scrollable tables and code blocks.</li>
    <li>Labels form controls and provides useful error messages and live result announcements in tools.</li>
    <li>Provides the Mermaid source as a text alternative when a diagram is rendered.</li>
    <li>Does not rely on color alone to communicate status in its own interface.</li>
    <li>Provides print styles for articles.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known limitations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Mermaid diagrams are SVG representations of structured relationships.
      Their internal reading order may not fully communicate the diagram’s
      meaning. The source is available, and essential explanations should be in
      prose as well.
    </li>
    <li>
      Some tool results update visually. Live regions announce them, but rapid
      updates can be verbose for screen-reader users. You can change inputs less
      frequently or use the copy/download output.
    </li>
    <li>
      Native date, time, and color pickers vary in accessibility across
      browsers and operating systems.
    </li>
    <li>
      Large reference tables can be cumbersome on small screens; they are
      scrollable and retain table semantics.
    </li>
    <li>
      Optional third-party analysis or advertising is disabled by default. If
      enabled, those services are outside ORIZ.IN’s full control.
    </li>
    <li>
      The site has not undergone a formal external accessibility audit. Manual
      keyboard checks and automated build checks reduce risk but do not prove
      conformance.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Feedback</h2>
  <p>
    If you encounter an accessibility barrier, email
    <a href={`mailto:${PROFILE.email}?subject=Accessibility`}>{PROFILE.email}</a>
    with the page URL, the browser and assistive technology you use, and what
    happened. Please describe the barrier precisely; “the page is inaccessible”
    is hard to act on.
  </p>
  <p>
    Related: <a href="/contact/">contact</a> and
    <a href="/corrections/">corrections</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
